# ============================================================
# Hermes Agent .gitignore
# ============================================================
# IMPORTANT (2026-06-08 portability audit):
#   The following heavy blobs are NOT in git because of size:
#     - portable-python/  (~230 MB, embedded Python 3.12.10)
#     - runtime/          (~700 MB, llama.cpp + CUDA DLLs + Node 23)
#     - data/models/*.gguf (multi-GB model files)
#   A fresh `git clone` therefore does NOT run on its own. The user
#   must follow the "Fresh install on a new PC" section in README.md
#   which runs `bin\setup-portable.bat` to fetch these via aria2
#   (or downloads them from the GitHub release assets).
#
#   If you want a single-double-click "plug and play" experience,
#   publish portable-python + runtime as GitHub release assets and
#   have setup-portable.bat download from there. See §16 in AGENTS.md.
# ============================================================

# --- Portable runtime (heavy, downloaded by setup-portable.bat) ---
portable-python/
runtime/
# Deps junctions to runtime content (don't commit through them):
deps/python-test/         # symlink to portable-python (test copy)
deps/tools/               # symlink to runtime tools (aria2c, gopeed)
deps/node/                # symlink to runtime/node23 (Node.js)
deps/llamacpp/            # mostly empty stub; junction content is in runtime/

# --- Upstream clean copy: hermes-agent (clone separately; tracked upstream) ---
# `hermes-agent/` is a giant clean copy of the NousResearch/hermes-agent
# upstream (Agent core / CLI). It is tracked upstream and we just clone
# it into our workspace. The local copy is NEVER committed here because:
#   1. It is ~5000 files
#   2. It is READ-ONLY for us (we modify in `modules/` not here)
#   3. Upstream `git pull` would conflict with our local edits
#   4. It is versioned upstream; pinning it in this repo would
#      duplicate state that is already canonically versioned elsewhere.
# To get a working copy, run:
#     git clone https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent.git hermes-agent
hermes-agent/

# Note: the EKKOLearnAI/hermes-web-ui WebUI is NOT a sibling clone anymore
# (2026-06-15a). The runtime copy lives at runtime/node23/node_modules/
# hermes-web-ui/ and is installed via `npm install -g hermes-web-ui` from
# runtime/node23/. No dev-source folder is needed.

# --- Data directories (user state; never commit) ---
# All per-user state lives under data/ and hermes/data/. Even though
# some files were committed before these rules were added, they are
# EXCLUDED from future tracking (see `git rm --cached` in commit log).
hermes/data/
hermes/data/nextchat/
tests/hermes/data/
# IMPORTANT (2026-06-13 fix): use `data/**` (not `data/`) so the
# `!data/models/*` negation below can actually re-include files in
# data/models/. With the old `data/` pattern, git's "parent dir
# excluded" rule blocks all negations under data/, and *nothing*
# under data/models/ could be tracked (router-preset.example.ini and
# 初始模型下载.bat were silently dropped in commit 8e9de8bf).
data/**
!data/models/
!data/models/*
data/models/*.gguf
data/models/*.bin
# user-specific NGL/ctx per model (do not commit the real one;
# data/models/router-preset.example.ini is the template)
data/models/router-preset.ini
data/hermes-agent/                   # webui state, auth, sessions, kanban
data/webui/                          # webui home, sqlite, secret key
data/memory/                         # chat memory store
data/knowledge/                      # knowledge base index
data/skills/                         # user-installed skills
data/kanban/                         # kanban boards/tasks/events
data/crons/                          # cron jobs
data/logs/                           # runtime logs

# --- Configuration & secrets (never commit) ---
.env
.env.*
.envrc
*.env.local
.webui_secret_key
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# --- Backups, dumps, runtime caches ---
*.bak
*.backup
*.dump
*.corrupt.*.bak
config.yaml.corrupt.*.bak
# HERMES_ROOT cache (atomic write, written by bin/hermes-root.py persist)
.hermes-root
# NOTE: .githooks/ is intentionally NOT ignored here -- the versioned
#       git hooks in this directory are meant to be tracked so they
#       ship with the repo (see bin/install-git-hooks.bat).

# --- Qoder / opencode IDE state ---
.qoder/
.opencode/
.opencode/tmp/

# --- Local agent plans / specs (workspace artifacts, never commit) ---
# mavis agent plan workspace
.mavis/
# trae AI assistant rules/specs
.trae/

# --- Python build artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.so
*.egg
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Node artifacts ---
node_modules/
.npm/
.yarn/
.pnpm-store/

# --- Logs & temp files ---
*.log
logs/
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.bak
.tmp/

# --- Editor & IDE state ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
.history/
*.code-workspace

# --- Diagnostic / scratch files generated by the agent itself ---
.git_status.txt
.git_tracked.txt
*.diag*
.tmp.*

# --- DWG / DXF tooling outputs and scratch (2026-06-16c) ---
# tools/ is committed (README.md + dwg/ + oda_setup.exe are real project assets);
# the *outputs* of those tools and the throwaway scratch scripts are not.
# (Inline `#` comments after a rule are NOT supported by git's .gitignore
# syntax and were silently breaking the rules below; keep them bare.)
dxf_conversion_log/
tools/_scratch/
tools/dwg/_archive/
tools/_find_*.ps1

# --- Docker ---
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile.local

# --- OS / shell artifacts ---
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
.Trashes
.Spotlight-V100
.fseventsd

# --- Misc build/test outputs ---
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.tsbuildinfo
.rollup.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
upstream/

# --- CodeGraph (dead end on Node 23.11 — keeps trying to be installed) ---
deps/codegraph/
bin/.codegraph/

# --- GitNexus external (installed in user HOME, not in repo) ---
.claude/
*.code-workspace
package-lock.json
bin/desktop.ini
config.yaml.pre-gitnexus.*.bak
